.policy "ruff-d103-undocumented-public-function" revision 2
.description "Document each public Python function with a docstring describing its behavior, arguments and return value."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff D103 (pydocstyle): a public module-level function with no docstring. Public: the module is, the
// function is listed in `__all__` when there is one, and its name does not start with `_`. `@overload`
// signatures, defs decorated with a `pydocstyle.ignore-decorators` entry and `.pyi` stubs are not checked.
//   def run(): pass            ← D103 at `run`
//   @overload
//   def run(x: int): ...       not reported
#include "python/docstrings.rr"

.violation D103(at: node, x: symbol) code "D103"
    "Add a docstring as the first statement of function `{x}`, describing what it does, its arguments and its return value."
    suppress ruff "D103"
D103(nm, x) :- doc_missing(_, "function", nm, x).